opam-version: "2.0"
name: "csilgen-transport"
version: "0.1.0-dev"
synopsis: "Canonical-CBOR transport library for the CSIL transport family"
description: """
Hand-written, dependency-free OCaml implementation of the CSIL transport wire
(the conventions doc plus the RPC, Events, and Datagrams specs): a canonical CBOR
codec, the tag-24 / status / version conventions, a bring-your-own carrier seam
(a record of closures), and matched client/server pairs for all three transports.

All I/O is synchronous and blocking — no Lwt/Async/Eio; the host owns the I/O loop
and threads. The library uses only the stdlib plus the bundled `unix` (for the UDP
carrier); the conformance test target is stdlib-only.

TODO: not yet published to opam-repository. To publish, add this package to
ocaml/opam-repository (or a private opam-repo) so consumers can
`opam install csilgen-transport` without a pin. Until then, consume via
`opam pin --subpath transports/ocaml ...` or dune `(vendored_dirs ...)` — see README.
"""
maintainer: "Catalyst Community"
authors: "Catalyst Community"
license: "Apache-2.0"
homepage: "https://github.com/catalystcommunity/csilgen"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/catalystcommunity/csilgen/issues"
dev-repo: "git+https://github.com/catalystcommunity/csilgen.git"
depends: [
  "ocaml" {>= "4.08"}
  "dune" {>= "3.0"}
]
build: [
  # Tests are not built under opam: the conformance vectors live at
  # transports/conformance/, outside this package directory, so they are run from
  # the repo via run-tests.sh, not via `opam install --with-test`.
  ["dune" "build" "-p" name "-j" jobs]
]
